# Repo-wide line-ending normalization. Git decides text vs binary per file
# by inspecting its content (looking for NUL bytes etc.), so this stays
# correct for new files without needing an extension added here by hand.
# Text files are stored in the repo with LF and converted to the local
# platform's line ending on checkout; binary files are never touched.
* text=auto

# Some fixture files under tests/testthat/fixtures/ are hashed byte-for-byte
# (file_hash = md5sum of the raw file), so those specific formats must never
# have their bytes altered even if Git's content-based auto-detection were
# ever to misjudge them. pdf/zip are unambiguous; omv and jasp are Java/ZIP
# archives despite their extension, so they need the same explicit override.
# Marking a binary format as text makes Git rewrite \r\n/\n byte sequences
# inside the binary data on checkout, which is what produced phantom
# "modified" diffs on Windows machines with core.autocrlf set.
*.pdf -text
*.zip -text
*.omv -text
*.jasp -text
